{title: My Soul Thirsts}
{subtitle: Psalms 42:2–3; 63:2}
{key: C}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [C] | [C] |
| [C] | [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
As the deer longs for water
[Bb]So my soul longs for [C]you
My soul thirsts for the [Bb]living God
[F]When can I come to [C]you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Yeshu, Yes[Bb]hu, [F]my soul thirsts for [C]you
Yeshu, Yes[Bb]hu, [F]my soul longs for [C]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
In a dry and weary land
[Bb]Where no water [C]is
Early I will seek [Bb]your face
[F]My soul is [C]yours
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Yeshu, Yes[Bb]hu, [F]my soul thirsts for [C]you
Yeshu, [Bb]Yeshu, [F]my soul longs for [C]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
My soul thirsts for [Bb][F][C]you
{end_of_verse}
